From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:49:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] irqchip: Add the interrupt controller of the FonTamSOC

The controller, driven through hwdrvirqctrl.h, a copy of the driver of
the FonTamSOC, dispatches the interrupts of its sources, one at a time,
to the harts, raising their machine external interrupt until
acknowledged, and their interprocessor interrupts, which ipi_mux
multiplexes. Device interrupts go to the boot hart only. The controller
also resets the system, which the restart handler requests: the
bootloader, resident, then loads the kernel again.

include/soc/fontamsoc/hwdrv.h provides the drivers of the FonTamSOC
with the environment which they expect from its operating system,
underLineOS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
